From 750ea0b8ec07d45a389c04b961ad3fa3c9c242f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:44:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the end of the HDR signalling that the driver
 refused is asked for again, bounded

When a video stops, SetHDR() without a picture takes HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA
away in the request, with a modeset. Where a change of the resolution
follows, that request is the one of the change of mode: the end of the HDR
signalling waits for it (CModeChangeHold, STOP), and on a dual-mode
DisplayPort connector the change goes out with the head turned off and on.
If the driver refuses that commit, or its test (CDRMAtomic then sends the
frame with the request before it), the display keeps the HDR signalling.
CHDRSignal::Settle() then makes the state of Kodi what the kernel has (HDR),
which is right, but nothing asked for the end again: a change of mode that
the driver refused is asked for again alone (CModesetRetry), without what
the refused request carried with it. The GUI went on with HDR signalling,
and the colorimetry of the video, until the next video. CroqueMr's R1.0.0
RC3 Preview, update 2, fixed a case with the same outcome in his own
clean-up after a video ("stopping playback during a resolution change could
leave HDR signaling active"); this is the case of Hades, found by following
that.

CHDRSignal::EndRetry follows the end of the signalling from its request
until the kernel has it, and asks for it again where the driver refused it,
with the pacing of a refused change of mode: with the next two frames, then
every two seconds, six commits of it in all. It waits while a change of mode
waits to be asked for again (the mode goes out alone first, then the end: a
driver that refuses both in one commit takes each alone), and while native
Dolby Vision has the output or the output is meant to be off. A video that
starts stops it. CWinSystemGbm::AskHDREndAgain(), before each commit of the
ordinary output, makes the request of the end of a video again (SetHDR()
without a picture: no HDR metadata, no HDR10+ InfoFrame, the depth of the
link for the GUI) with the colorimetry that Kodi asked for last
(RequeueOutputProperties()). The log says when the end is refused, when it
went out after refusals, and when it is given up.

Host test (hdrend_test.cpp, the model of CDRMAtomic and of the kernel of
hdrsettle_test, with CHDRSignal and CModesetRetry as the tree has them):
nine cases, among them the end refused together with the change of mode
and taken after it, refused twice, always refused (given up after five
more), a video that starts meanwhile or right after the mode, native Dolby Vision and the output
off. Against the headers before, the cases of a refused end fail; four
mutations each make it fail. hdrsettle_test and hdrsignal_test pass
unchanged. Not run on a graphics card.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/HDRSignal.h      | 102 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp |  56 +++++++++++++++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h   |   7 ++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.h  |   2 +
 4 files changed, 167 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/HDRSignal.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/HDRSignal.h
index bbee1de..f906a60 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/HDRSignal.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/HDRSignal.h
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 
 #pragma once
 
+#include "drm/DRMModesetRetry.h"
 #include "utils/DisplayInfo.h"
 
 #include <cstdint>
@@ -271,6 +272,107 @@ public:
     return true;
   }
 
+  /*!
+   * \brief Hades: the end of the HDR signalling that the driver refused is asked for again, bounded
+   *
+   * A commit that carries the end of a video's HDR signalling (HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA taken away:
+   * SetHDR() without a picture) and that the driver refuses, or whose test it refuses (CDRMAtomic
+   * then sends the frame with the request before it), leaves the display in HDR. Settle() then
+   * makes the state of Kodi what the kernel has, HDR, and nothing asked for the end again: the GUI
+   * went on with HDR signalling until the next video. That is likelier where a video stops during a
+   * change of the resolution, whose commit carries both: the end of the signalling waits for the
+   * change of mode to the GUI (CModeChangeHold, STOP), and on a dual-mode DisplayPort connector a
+   * change of mode goes out with the head turned off and on. A change of mode that the driver
+   * refused is asked for again alone (CModesetRetry), without what the refused request carried
+   * with it. (CroqueMr's R1.0.0 RC3 Preview, update 2, fixed a case of the same outcome in his own
+   * clean-up after a video; this one is Hades'.)
+   *
+   * Here the end is asked for again (CWinSystemGbm::AskHDREndAgain()) with the pacing of a refused
+   * change of mode: with the next two frames, then every two seconds, six commits of it in all.
+   * Not while a change of mode waits to be asked for again (the mode goes out alone first, then the
+   * end of the signalling: a driver that refuses both in one commit takes each alone), nor while
+   * native Dolby Vision has the output (its end restores the output its own way), nor while the
+   * output is meant to be off. A request of SetHDR() with a picture (a video that starts) stops it,
+   * as one that finds nothing to take away does. This class only decides.
+   */
+  class EndRetry
+  {
+  public:
+    using Clock = CModesetRetry::Clock;
+    enum class Then
+    {
+      NOTHING, //!< nothing that is followed here
+      TAKEN, //!< the kernel has no HDR signalling
+      AGAIN, //!< refused: asked for again later
+      GIVEN_UP, //!< refused the last time: not asked for again until the next end
+    };
+
+    //! A request of SetHDR() (not the one that asks for the end again): picture, it has one;
+    //! cleared, it takes the HDR signalling away (Outcome::cleared)
+    void Requested(bool picture, bool cleared)
+    {
+      m_waiting = false;
+      if (!picture && cleared)
+        m_retry.Asked();
+      else
+        m_retry.Forget();
+    }
+
+    //! What Settle() found once the request that carried a change was finished: asked, the value
+    //! that the request queued (m_queuedHdrMetadata before Settle()); kernel, the one after it
+    Then Found(Settled settled,
+               std::optional<uint64_t> asked,
+               std::optional<uint64_t> kernel,
+               Clock::time_point now)
+    {
+      if (settled == Settled::NOTHING)
+        return Then::NOTHING;
+      m_waiting = false;
+      if (asked.value_or(0) != 0)
+      {
+        // (a request with HDR settled: no end is followed)
+        m_retry.Forget();
+        return Then::NOTHING;
+      }
+      switch (m_retry.Result(kernel.value_or(0) == 0, now))
+      {
+        case CModesetRetry::Outcome::TAKEN:
+          return Then::TAKEN;
+        case CModesetRetry::Outcome::AGAIN:
+          return Then::AGAIN;
+        case CModesetRetry::Outcome::GIVEN_UP:
+          return Then::GIVEN_UP;
+        case CModesetRetry::Outcome::NONE:
+          break;
+      }
+      return Then::NOTHING;
+    }
+
+    //! Whether the end is asked for again with the frame that is about to be committed: nativeOutput,
+    //! native Dolby Vision has the output; active, the output is meant to be on; modeWaits, a
+    //! change of mode that the driver refused waits to be asked for again (CModesetRetry::Pending())
+    bool AsksAgain(Clock::time_point now, bool nativeOutput, bool active, bool modeWaits) const
+    {
+      return !m_waiting && !nativeOutput && active && !modeWaits && m_retry.Due(now);
+    }
+
+    //! The end was asked for again; queued: a change of HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA is in the request
+    //! (none could be queued: nothing more is asked)
+    void AskedAgain(bool queued)
+    {
+      if (queued)
+        m_waiting = true;
+      else
+        m_retry.Forget();
+    }
+
+    unsigned int Refusals() const { return m_retry.Refusals(); }
+
+  private:
+    CModesetRetry m_retry;
+    bool m_waiting = false; //!< asked for again, and not settled yet
+  };
+
 private:
   // The state before a change, unless one is kept already (the kernel still has that one); the
   // change goes in the request of this generation
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
index 6a14f67..c5161cb 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
@@ -2920,6 +2920,9 @@ void CWinSystemGbm::FlipPage(bool rendered, bool videoLayer, bool async)
 {
   // Hades: what the commits before this one did with a change of the HDR signalling
   SettleHDR();
+  // Hades: ... and the end of it that the driver refused, asked for again with this frame
+  // (CHDRSignal::EndRetry)
+  AskHDREndAgain();
 
   if (m_videoLayerBridge && !videoLayer)
   {
@@ -4247,6 +4250,10 @@ bool CWinSystemGbm::SetHDR(const VideoPicture* videoPicture)
   const CHDRSignal::Outcome outcome =
       CHDRSignal::Request(m_eotf, m_hdrBlob, m_queuedHdrMetadata, want, display, !videoPicture,
                           request, &m_hdrBefore, drm->RequestGeneration());
+  // Hades: the end of the HDR signalling is followed until the kernel has it; a video that starts
+  // stops that (CHDRSignal::EndRetry). Not for the request that asks for it again.
+  if (!m_hdrEndAgain)
+    m_hdrEndRetry.Requested(videoPicture != nullptr, outcome.cleared);
   if (CHDRSignal::Tell(want, outcome, m_hdrTold))
     CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "HDR output: no HDR signalling for this {} video: {}",
               eotf == KODI::UTILS::Eotf::HLG ? "HLG" : "PQ", CHDRSignal::Why(outcome.reason));
@@ -4476,6 +4483,8 @@ void CWinSystemGbm::SettleHDR()
     return;
   const auto* connector = drm->GetConnector();
   const KODI::UTILS::Eotf asked = m_eotf;
+  // (Hades: what the request asked for, for CHDRSignal::EndRetry)
+  const std::optional<uint64_t> askedValue = m_queuedHdrMetadata;
   const auto settled =
       CHDRSignal::Settle(m_eotf, m_hdrBlob, m_queuedHdrMetadata, m_hdrBefore,
                          drm->RequestGeneration(),
@@ -4501,6 +4510,53 @@ void CWinSystemGbm::SettleHDR()
               "HDR output: the connector has other HDR metadata than Kodi asked for ({}): the state "
               "of Kodi is what it has ({})",
               name(asked), name(m_eotf));
+  // Hades: the end of the HDR signalling, refused, is asked for again (AskHDREndAgain())
+  switch (m_hdrEndRetry.Found(settled, askedValue, m_queuedHdrMetadata,
+                              CHDRSignal::EndRetry::Clock::now()))
+  {
+    case CHDRSignal::EndRetry::Then::AGAIN:
+      if (m_hdrEndRetry.Refusals() == 1)
+        CLog::Log(LOGWARNING,
+                  "HDR output: the end of the HDR signalling was refused, and the display still "
+                  "signals HDR: it is asked for again with the next frames, then every {} s, {} "
+                  "times in all (after a change of mode that waits, if one does)",
+                  CModesetRetry::SPACING.count() / 1000, CModesetRetry::ATTEMPTS);
+      break;
+    case CHDRSignal::EndRetry::Then::GIVEN_UP:
+      CLog::Log(LOGERROR,
+                "HDR output: the end of the HDR signalling was refused {} times: given up, the "
+                "display signals HDR until the next video or the next change of the output",
+                m_hdrEndRetry.Refusals());
+      break;
+    case CHDRSignal::EndRetry::Then::TAKEN:
+      if (m_hdrEndRetry.Refusals())
+        CLog::Log(LOGINFO,
+                  "HDR output: the end of the HDR signalling went out after {} refusal(s): the "
+                  "display signals no HDR",
+                  m_hdrEndRetry.Refusals());
+      break;
+    case CHDRSignal::EndRetry::Then::NOTHING:
+      break;
+  }
+}
+
+void CWinSystemGbm::AskHDREndAgain()
+{
+  const auto drm = std::dynamic_pointer_cast<CDRMAtomic>(m_DRM);
+  if (!drm || !m_hdrEndRetry.AsksAgain(CHDRSignal::EndRetry::Clock::now(), NativeDVOutputInUse(),
+                                       drm->IsActive(), drm->ModesetRetryPending()))
+    return;
+  CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "HDR output: the end of the HDR signalling is asked for again ({} refused)",
+            m_hdrEndRetry.Refusals());
+  // As at the end of a video: no HDR metadata, no HDR10+ InfoFrame, the depth of the link for the
+  // GUI (SetHDR()), and the colorimetry that Kodi asked for last, which the refused request
+  // carried too (RequeueOutputProperties(), with a modeset)
+  m_hdrEndAgain = true;
+  SetHDR(nullptr);
+  m_hdrEndAgain = false;
+  if (m_hdrBefore)
+    RequeueOutputProperties();
+  m_hdrEndRetry.AskedAgain(m_hdrBefore.has_value());
 }
 
 std::shared_ptr<const KODI::UTILS::CDisplayInfo> CWinSystemGbm::DisplayInfo() const
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h
index 76ddd04..f98d620 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h
@@ -299,6 +299,9 @@ protected:
   //! (CHDRSignal::Settle()): a commit that the driver refused left the output as it was. From the
   //! thread that draws.
   void SettleHDR();
+  //! Hades: the end of the HDR signalling that the driver refused, asked for again with the frame
+  //! that is about to be committed, where CHDRSignal::EndRetry says so. From the thread that draws.
+  void AskHDREndAgain();
   //! \brief A video is being set up, the output is being put back after one, or its mode is
   //! being set: the outputs are not looked at for a while after it (CDRMDisplayWatch). From
   //! the thread that draws.
@@ -759,6 +762,10 @@ private:
   std::optional<CHDRSignal::Reason> m_hdrTold;
   //! Hades: the state before a change of it that is not known to have gone out (SettleHDR())
   std::optional<CHDRSignal::Before<CDRMPropertyBlob>> m_hdrBefore;
+  //! Hades: ... and the end of the HDR signalling, followed until the kernel has it, and asked for
+  //! again where the driver refused it (CHDRSignal::EndRetry, AskHDREndAgain())
+  CHDRSignal::EndRetry m_hdrEndRetry;
+  bool m_hdrEndAgain = false; //!< SetHDR() is the request that asks for the end again
   //! Hades: HDR10+ (SetHDR10Plus()): what is queued, and the blobs of the last payloads, kept
   //! while a request that falls back may still name them
   CHDR10PlusOutput m_hdr10Plus;
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.h
index 7f36315..a9a3845 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.h
@@ -72,6 +72,8 @@ public:
   //! Hades: a change of mode that the driver kept refusing was given up since the last question
   //! (CModesetRetry)
   bool TakeModesetGivenUp() override { return std::exchange(m_modesetGivenUp, false); }
+  //! Hades: a change of mode that the driver refused waits to be asked for again (CModesetRetry)
+  bool ModesetRetryPending() const { return m_modesetRetry.Pending(); }
   //! Hades: the next commit would carry more than a framebuffer: properties added since the last
   //! one, or a modeset that is pending
   bool HasPendingRequest() const { return m_need_modeset || (m_req && !m_req->Empty()); }
-- 
